---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const schema = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'NoCharge Help', description: 'Practical help for starting, controlling, and troubleshooting NoCharge games.', url: 'https://nocharge.net/help/' },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://nocharge.net/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Help', item: 'https://nocharge.net/help/' },
  ] },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Help" description="Practical help for starting, controlling, and troubleshooting NoCharge games." path="/help/" schema={schema}>
  <div class="help-page">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Help' }]} />
    <header><picture class="help-art"><source srcset="/editorial-art/help-800.webp 800w, /editorial-art/help-1200.webp 1200w, /editorial-art/help-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 58rem) calc(100vw - 2rem), 58rem" type="image/webp" /><img src="/editorial-art/help-1600.jpg" srcset="/editorial-art/help-800.jpg 800w, /editorial-art/help-1200.jpg 1200w, /editorial-art/help-1600.jpg 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 58rem) calc(100vw - 2rem), 58rem" alt="" width="1600" height="900" /></picture><p class="eyebrow">Player support</p><h1 class="page-title">Get back to the game.</h1><p class="lede">A practical guide to controls, local progress, and the few things worth checking when a browser behaves differently.</p></header>
    <div class="help-grid">
      <section class="panel help-section"><h2>Starting and controlling a game</h2><ul><li>Open a game from the <a href="/arcade/">Arcade</a> and use Start or the first available board control.</li><li>Restart with <strong>New game</strong> in the shared game toolbar.</li><li>Use the toolbar to pause and Resume. Switching tabs pauses active play; returning resumes only when the game was not manually paused.</li><li>Game pages document keyboard controls. Touch and pointer controls are available where the game supports them.</li><li>Mute is persistent in this browser. Fullscreen or immersive mode depends on the browser and device permission.</li></ul></section>
      <section class="panel help-section"><h2>Scores and local data</h2><p>Best results and game progress are stored in this browser on this device. No account or cloud sync is involved, so a different browser will not have the same local data.</p><p>Use <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> to clear game data. Clearing game data does not change your separate analytics consent choice.</p><p><a href="/">Recently Played</a> records a small local list after meaningful play so you can return to a game.</p></section>
      <section class="panel help-section"><h2>My Arcade</h2><p><a href="/my-arcade/">My Arcade</a> gathers what this browser has already saved: the games you last played, each game’s own best result or progress, and links back into the game and its guide. It is not an account, and there is no single score across different games.</p><p>It will look different in another browser, another profile, a private window, or another device, because the underlying values are stored only where you played. A game with nothing saved simply says so.</p><p>Clear the data with the <a href="/privacy/#local-data">Clear game data</a> control on Privacy or the matching control on My Arcade; both remove the same game keys and leave your analytics consent choice alone.</p><p>Opening My Arcade does not count as playing. Recently Played is written only after a real action inside a game, so viewing the dashboard never changes its order or timestamps.</p></section>
      <section class="panel help-section"><h2>When something does not work</h2><ul><li>Reload the page and make sure the browser is current.</li><li>If a game does not load, confirm JavaScript is enabled, review whether a browser extension is blocking the game, and optionally try a private window or another current browser.</li><li>If sound differs, check the device volume, browser tab mute, and the game mute control.</li><li>If fullscreen behaves differently, use the browser’s own fullscreen permission or continue in the normal view.</li><li>If a layout or control is difficult to use, email an accessibility report with the page, browser, device type, and what happened.</li></ul></section>
      <section class="panel help-section"><h2>Setup and input choices</h2><p>If zoom, a keyboard layout, pointer, stand, or low-noise desk question is getting in the way, <a href="/setup/">Quiet Setup</a> compares practical options and begins with no-purchase adjustments. It is editorial guidance, separate from game controls and gameplay.</p></section>
      <section class="panel help-section"><h2>Need to report a problem?</h2><p>For a broken game, accessibility problem, privacy question, or problematic advertisement, contact <a href="mailto:hello@nocharge.net">hello@nocharge.net</a>. Please do not send passwords or sensitive personal information.</p><p>Advertising and analytics are separate choices. Games remain playable when optional analytics is declined. See <a href="/advertising/">Advertising</a> and <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> for the relevant explanations.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.help-art{display:block;aspect-ratio:16/9;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius);margin-bottom:1.25rem}.help-art img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.help-page{display:grid;gap:2.5rem;max-width:58rem;margin-inline:auto}.help-page>header{max-width:48rem}.help-grid{display:grid;gap:1rem}.help-section{padding:1.25rem}.help-section h2{font-size:1.25rem;letter-spacing:-.025em}.help-section p,.help-section li{color:var(--muted)}.help-section p+p{margin-top:.8rem}.help-section ul{display:grid;gap:.55rem;margin:.85rem 0 0;padding-left:1.2rem}.help-section a{color:var(--accent-strong);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}@media(min-width:48rem){.help-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
